<title>USA: NY business loans down $176 mln in Jan 1 week.</title>
<headline>NY business loans down $176 mln in Jan 1 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commercial and industrial loans at the six major New York banks, excluding acceptances, fell $176 million to $43,316 million in the week ended January 1, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York said.</p>
<p>Including acceptances, loans fell $177 million to $43,553 million.</p>
<p>Commercial paper outstanding nationally fell $4,036 million to $778,162 million.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
